course: dictionary
lesson: 4965
title: Front teeth: the incisor
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: An incisor is one of the sharp, flat front teeth you use to bite and cut food. You can work out the meaning from the words around it. «There are different teeth for different jobs: sharp incisors at the front cut, pointed canines tear, and wide molars at the back grind.» The list tells you incisors are the sharp teeth at the front that cut.
explain: «Incisors at the front cut food.» The words front and cut are your clues. Swap in your meaning: "sharp, flat front teeth that cut food" still makes sense, so you have it right.
explain: Look for the job a word does, too. Canines tear and molars grind, so incisors must be the ones that cut. Your first baby teeth are usually incisors, so you have probably been using them since you were a baby.
fact: Incisor means one of the sharp, flat front teeth used for biting and cutting food.
fact: Humans have four types of teeth: incisors for cutting, canines for tearing, and premolars and molars for grinding.
fact: A grown-up has 8 incisors, four on top and four on the bottom.
fact: «Mice have four front teeth, the incisors, which keep growing all their lives» and are worn down by gnawing.
fact: Rabbits, guinea pigs, rats, squirrels and beavers also have front teeth that never stop growing.
exercise: «Incisors at the front cut food.» What is an incisor? | *A sharp, flat front tooth used for cutting food | A back tooth used for grinding food | A claw used for digging | A bone in the jaw
exercise: «There are different teeth for different jobs: sharp incisors at the front cut, pointed canines tear, and wide molars at the back grind.» Which teeth are used for tearing? | Molars | *Canines | Incisors | Premolars
exercise: «A grown-up set has 8 incisors for cutting, 4 canines for gripping, 8 premolars and 12 molars for grinding.» How many incisors does a grown-up set have? | 4 | 12 | *8 | 20
test: «The front teeth, or incisors, of rabbits and guinea pigs grow all their lives and are worn down by chewing tough grass and hay.» What are the front teeth of rabbits called? | Premolars | Canines | *Incisors | Molars
test: Which job does an incisor do? | *Cutting and biting food | Gripping slippery food | Tearing meat into strips | Grinding food into a paste
exam: Read «Mice have four front teeth, the incisors, which keep growing all their lives.» What is the best meaning of incisors here? | Teeth at the back for grinding | Bones in the jaw | Claws used for digging | *Sharp front teeth that cut and bite
